   ],
   "question": "Using the trapezoidal rule with 3 function values, find an approximation to the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 e^{(\\ln 3)x}\\,dx$, leaving your answer in exact form.",
   "answer": "$e^{(\\ln 3)x} = 3^x$. Function values at $x = 0, \\frac12, 1$ ($h = \\frac12$): $1, \\sqrt3, 3$.\n$$\\int_0^1 3^x\\,dx \\approx \\frac{1}{4}\\left[1 + 2\\sqrt3 + 3\\right] = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt3}{2}.$$"
